---
import TreatmentPage from "../../../components/TreatmentPage.astro";

const page = {
  "slug": "ovulation-test",
  "name": "Ovulation Test",
  "title": "Ovulation Test in Lahore | Check If You Are Ovulating",
  "description": "Ovulation test in Lahore: LH kits, progesterone blood test and ultrasound tracking to check if and when you ovulate. Explained by Dr. Kamran Saleem.",
  "eyebrow": "Ovulation Test",
  "h1": "Ovulation Test in Lahore",
  "waText": "Hello, I would like to book a consultation about the Ovulation Test with Dr. Kamran Saleem.",
  "ctaLabel": "Book a fertility consultation",
  "heroSub": "An ovulation test checks whether you release an egg each cycle and when your fertile window falls. Irregular or absent ovulation is one of the most common and most treatable causes of infertility. Dr. Kamran Saleem uses the simplest reliable method for your situation.",
  "leadIn": [
    {
      "rich": [
        "This is part of our ",
        [
          "Fertility Assessment & Diagnosis",
          "/services/assessment"
        ],
        ". Tests are recommended only when they are clinically appropriate and likely to guide your next step."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-an-ovulation-test",
      "title": "What Is an Ovulation Test?",
      "intro": "Several different tests answer two questions.",
      "icon": "flask",
      "body": [
        "The first question is whether you ovulate at all. The second is when, so intercourse or treatment can be timed. Home kits, blood tests and ultrasound each answer these in different ways."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "your-fertile-window",
      "title": "Your Fertile Window",
      "intro": "It is shorter than most people expect.",
      "icon": "user",
      "body": [
        "The fertile window is roughly the five days before ovulation plus the day of ovulation. Ovulation usually happens about 14 days before the next period, so in a long or irregular cycle the date moves later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ways-to-test-for-ovulation",
      "title": "Ways to Test for Ovulation",
      "intro": "Each method has strengths and limits.",
      "icon": "calendar",
      "body": [
        {
          "ul": [
            "Urine LH kits: detect the LH surge 24 to 48 hours before ovulation, useful for timing",
            "Mid-luteal progesterone blood test: taken about 7 days before the expected period, confirms that ovulation happened",
            "Ultrasound follicle tracking: the most precise method, showing the follicle grow and rupture",
            "Cycle charting and cervical mucus: free, but less reliable on their own",
            "Basal body temperature: shows that ovulation has already happened, so it is poor for timing"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "how-to-use-lh-kits",
      "title": "How to Use LH Kits",
      "intro": "Used well, they are simple and effective.",
      "icon": "heart",
      "body": [
        {
          "ul": [
            "Begin testing a few days before expected ovulation, around day 10 in a 28-day cycle, and adjust for your cycle length",
            "Test once or twice daily, ideally in the afternoon, without drinking a large amount beforehand",
            "A positive result means ovulation is likely within 24 to 48 hours, so have intercourse that day and the next",
            "Kits can mislead in PCOS, where baseline LH is high, and with very irregular cycles"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "when-ovulation-does-not-happen-regularly",
      "title": "When Ovulation Does Not Happen Regularly",
      "intro": "Common causes are treatable.",
      "icon": "compare",
      "body": [
        {
          "ul": [
            "PCOS",
            "Thyroid disease",
            "High prolactin",
            "Low body weight, intense exercise or stress (hypothalamic causes)",
            "Premature ovarian insufficiency or declining ovarian reserve",
            "Certain medicines"
          ]
        },
        {
          "rich": [
            "Hormone tests, such as prolactin and TSH, help find the cause. Treatment is described under ",
            [
              "ovulation induction & PCOS",
              "/services/fertility-treatment/ovulation-induction"
            ],
            "."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "when-tracking-is-not-enough",
      "title": "When Tracking Is Not Enough",
      "intro": "Know when to ask for help.",
      "icon": "shield",
      "body": [
        "If your periods are irregular or absent, if kits never show a surge, or if you have been trying for 12 months (6 months if over 35), a proper assessment is more useful than more tracking."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ovulation-test-cost-in-lahore",
      "title": "Ovulation Test Cost in Lahore",
      "intro": "Transparent fees.",
      "icon": "coin",
      "body": [
        "The consultation fee is shown before you confirm. Blood tests and ultrasound are priced separately and recommended only when they are likely to guide a decision."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "related-assessments",
      "title": "Related Assessments",
      "intro": "A fertility assessment is more than one test.",
      "icon": "flask",
      "body": [
        {
          "rich": [
            "Other parts of a fertility assessment: ",
            [
              "Female Fertility Test",
              "/services/assessment/female-fertility-test"
            ],
            ", ",
            [
              "Male Fertility Test",
              "/services/assessment/male-fertility-test"
            ],
            " and ",
            [
              "Hormonal Analysis",
              "/services/assessment/hormonal-analysis"
            ],
            "."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "How do I know if I am ovulating?",
      "a": "Regular cycles with mid-cycle changes suggest ovulation, but a mid-luteal progesterone blood test or follicle tracking on ultrasound confirms it."
    },
    {
      "q": "When should I use an ovulation kit?",
      "a": "A few days before you expect to ovulate, around day 10 in a 28-day cycle, adjusting for your cycle length."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why does my ovulation kit stay positive?",
      "a": "In PCOS the baseline LH is often high, which can cause repeated or persistent positive results even when ovulation is not happening."
    },
    {
      "q": "When is the progesterone test done?",
      "a": "About 7 days before your next expected period, which is day 21 in a 28-day cycle, and adjusted if your cycle is longer."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I ovulate without having a period?",
      "a": "Occasionally, but regular periods usually reflect regular ovulation, and absent periods usually mean ovulation is not happening."
    },
    {
      "q": "Are temperature charts reliable for timing?",
      "a": "They show that ovulation has already happened, so they are less useful for timing intercourse than LH kits or ultrasound."
    },
    {
      "q": "Are ovulation problems treatable?",
      "a": "Yes. Treatment depends on the cause and may include lifestyle changes, treating thyroid or prolactin problems, or ovulation induction medicines."
    },
    {
      "q": "How long should I try before getting help?",
      "a": "Twelve months if you are under 35, six months if you are over 35, and sooner if your periods are irregular or absent."
    }
  ],
  "closingHeading": "Ovulation Test in Lahore With Dr. Kamran Saleem",
  "closingParas": [
    "At Kamran Fertility Clinic, Dr. Kamran Saleem provides the ovulation test with 25 years of experience in male and female reproductive health, and explains every result in plain language.",
    "Investigations are recommended only when they are clinically appropriate, never as a routine package, and the aim is to find the cause before choosing any treatment.",
    "If you already have reports from elsewhere, bring them and we will review what is worth repeating."
  ],
  "resources": [
    {
      "href": "/resources/fertility-assessment-in-lahore",
      "category": "Fertility Treatment",
      "title": "Where Can You Get a Fertility Assessment in Lahore?"
    },
    {
      "href": "/resources/when-to-seek-fertility-consultation",
      "category": "Getting started",
      "title": "Fertility Consultation: When Should You Seek Advice?"
    },
    {
      "href": "/resources/pcos-and-fertility",
      "category": "Women's health",
      "title": "PCOS and Fertility: Can You Get Pregnant with PCOS?"
    }
  ],
  "close": {
    "heading": "Not Sure Which Tests You Need?",
    "body": "Bring any existing reports to your consultation, and we will explain what they mean and what, if anything, is worth doing next.",
    "cta": "Book a Consultation"
  }
};
---

<TreatmentPage {...page} />
